{
  "contractVersion": 1,
  "kind": "test-vectors",
  "subject": "jwt",
  "notes": [
    "HS256 verification, run against fast-servers/service-core/src/jwt.c and against jose. See contracts/AGENTS.md, *test-vectors*, for the shape and for what the two runners are.",
    "What is contracted is `expect`: whether the token is accepted, and the claim value that comes out of it. The reason a token was refused is not -- every refusal is one 401 with one body, so a caller cannot observe which one it was, and the two implementations check in a different order. `c.result` records the reason the C path reports because a log line carries it; it is asserted by the C runner alone.",
    "Every vector is wrong in at most one way. A token that is both expired and misaddressed would only pin whichever check happens to run first, which is not shared behaviour.",
    "`token` is derived: base64url(header) + \".\" + base64url(payload) + \".\" + base64url(HMAC-SHA256(secret, signed input)), with the last character of the signature flipped where `tamperSignature` is true. The TypeScript runner recomputes it from `header` and `payload` and fails if it disagrees, so an edited payload cannot silently keep a stale signature. `bun run regen:vectors` writes the tokens back.",
    "A vector whose `header` and `payload` are null carries a `token` that is not of that shape at all -- a malformed one -- and nothing is derived for it."
  ],
  "secret": {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "contract-vector-secret-not-a-real-one",
    "note": "A test secret and nothing else. It signs no real token anywhere."
  },
  "rules": {
    "algorithm": {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "HS256",
      "note": "The only algorithm either implementation accepts."
    },
    "claimMaxBytes": {
      "type": "uint32",
      "value": "127",
      "note": "Longest accepted claim value, terminator excluded. SC_JWT_MAX_CLAIM - 1 in service_core/jwt.h."
    },
    "expiryIsClosed": {
      "type": "bool",
      "value": "true",
      "note": "exp <= now is expired. Both implementations, see the two boundary vectors."
    }
  },
  "fields": {
    "id": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "Stable forever. A failure names this."
    },
    "why": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "What this vector is load bearing for."
    },
    "claimName": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "The claim the verifier is asked to copy out."
    },
    "issuer": {
      "type": "text",
      "nullable": true,
      "note": "Configured issuer, or null for a verifier configured without one."
    },
    "audience": {
      "type": "text",
      "nullable": true,
      "note": "As issuer."
    },
    "now": {
      "type": "int64",
      "unit": "unix_seconds",
      "note": "The instant the token is verified at, passed in rather than read off a clock."
    },
    "header": {
      "type": "text",
      "nullable": true,
      "note": "The JOSE header as exact bytes, not as an object: a vector has to be able to spell one that is not valid JSON."
    },
    "payload": {
      "type": "text",
      "nullable": true,
      "note": "As header."
    },
    "tamperSignature": {
      "type": "bool",
      "note": "Flip the last character of the signature."
    },
    "token": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "The token as it arrives over the wire. Derived; see notes."
    },
    "expect.accepted": {
      "type": "bool",
      "note": "The contract. Both implementations assert it."
    },
    "expect.claim": {
      "type": "text",
      "nullable": true,
      "note": "The claim value on acceptance, null on refusal. The contract."
    },
    "c.result": {
      "type": "text",
      "note": "The sc_jwt_result the C path reports. Diagnostic; the C runner asserts it, the TypeScript one does not."
    },
    "typescript": {
      "type": "text",
      "nullable": true,
      "note": "Present only where the TypeScript path cannot meet `expect`. Carries the outcome it produces instead and a `why`. The TypeScript runner asserts the divergence really happens, so one that gets fixed fails the suite until the block is deleted."
    }
  },
